const claims=c.QUESTION_QUALITY_ADVERSARIAL_CLAIMS,sources=c.QUESTION_QUALITY_ADVERSARIAL_SOURCES;
const lines=["# Adversarial correction sources - 2026-11-02","","Targeted, read-only factual checks under AGENTS.md. All 39 new atomic claims and 35 runtime source records remain `needs_clinician_review`. Authority and reuse rights are separate. Rechecked publications have new scope records but are not counted as independent publications merely because an older source ID exists. No source text, table, figure, algorithm, question-bank item or recalled item is retained.","","Runtime records: `packages/clinical-content/src/question-quality-adversarial-evidence-20261102.ts`. The original synthetic authoring worksheet and the claim mapping compiler are in `tools/question-quality`; they never retrieve sources during gameplay.","","## Limits and specific checks","","A02 compares specified filling/emptying/duct protocols, not a claim that every MRI/CT alternative is wrong after ultrasound. Melissa must confirm the exact ranking. A06 separates medication-associated secretion from the focal discharge component; age-specific imaging remains bound to the supplied adult female profiles. A25 uses the already verified named ART combination and newly verified route-specific midazolam rules. The NIH interaction table direct request returned 403; its search snippet was not treated as independent evidence.","","Chicago v4 directly supports the primary-position distinction and the failed-DCI threshold; B04's 30-80 readouts are explicitly synthetic values within that supported range. No device-specific IRP number, exact dose, clinical probability or wait duration was invented. Hypothetical trial margins and process counts are clearly constructed model/protocol inputs; the accompanying QA checks arithmetic, not clinical efficacy.","","ASCRS is the one adequately retrieved guideline for the new adverse-polyp application; AGA/ASGE requests failed, so they are not counted as corroboration. The supplied CT pathway is not contrasted against a valid CT-chest/abdominal-MRI pathway. Older ESSR technique guidance directly supports viable-area targeting; current ESSR/SEOM guidance supports MRI and planned cores. Current EADO guidance was read as a full public PDF; ESMO direct retrieval encountered captcha and is not used as the new factual anchor.","","Korean 2024/2025 and JGCA2021 support the B23 scope. The contradictory English JGCA2025 hilar wording recorded in the previous ledger remains WITHHELD; no station-10 teaching point was inferred. BSH and the independent gastric-MALT review support integrated classification and histologic response. ESGE2026 supports the ulcer modality comparison; its topical rescue/temporizing role is retained, rather than declaring powder never useful.","","Many PMC direct URLs returned captcha. Accessible publisher HTML or full official PDFs were used where available; bibliographic search records were used only to confirm metadata. Public availability is not inferred to grant a reuse license. No proprietary SCORE, commercial question bank, UpToDate, AccessSurgery, textbook corpus, paywalled snippet or incidental NCCN search hit was used.","","## Complete runtime source records",""];
for(const s of sources){lines.push("### "+s.id,"",s.completeCitation,"","- Organization/journal: "+s.organizationOrJournal,"- Authors: "+s.authors.join("; "),"- Year: "+(s.publicationYear??"undated, not inferred"),"- DOI: "+(s.doi??"none stated")+"; official/source URL: [source]("+s.officialUrl+").","- Access date: "+s.accessedOn+"; source class: `"+s.sourceClass+"`.","- License/reuse: "+s.licenseLabel+"; `"+s.reuseStatus+"`. "+s.reuseNotes,"- Authority/intended use ("+s.usageRole+"): "+s.authorityAssessment,"- Supported claim IDs: "+s.evidenceClaimIds.map(id=>"`"+id+"`").join(", "),"");}
lines.push("## Metadata-only correction check","","Stable ID: `source.qq20261102a.ata2025-corrigendum-check`. SAGE Publications. Corrigendum to: 2025 American Thyroid Association Management Guidelines for Adult Patients with Differentiated Thyroid Cancer. Thyroid. 2025;35(11):1350. doi:10.1177/10507256251387671. [Public correction](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13521431/). Accessed 2026-11-02. Class: correction; copyright SAGE, targeted verification only, no open reuse license inferred. No named byline is supplied. Intended use: verify whether the retrieved correction changes the preoperative ultrasound claim. It corrects affiliations/byline, not recommendation 7. Cross-check target: `claim.qq20261102a.papillary-cytology-regional-survey`; not counted as independent clinical evidence.","","## Atomic claims and limitations","","| Claim ID | Independently written statement | Supporting source IDs | Category / certainty | Limitation |","|---|---|---|---|---|");
for(const claim of claims)lines.push("| "+[claim.id,claim.statement,claim.sourceIds.join(", "),claim.evidenceCategory+" / "+claim.certainty,claim.limitation].map(cell).join(" | ")+" |");
lines.push("","Every listed claim has lastCheckedOn 2026-11-02 and needs_clinician_review. Review mapping is per exact question variant, never an approval of the underlying concept or a clinical release.","","## Exact question mappings","","| Review ID | Variant ID | Added claim IDs |","|---|---|---|");
for(const r of c.QUESTION_QUALITY_ADVERSARIAL_REVISIONS)lines.push("| "+[r.auditId,r.questionVariantId,r.question.supportingEvidenceClaimIds.filter(id=>id.startsWith("claim.qq20261102a.")).join(", ")].map(cell).join(" | ")+" |");
fs.writeFileSync("docs/research/sources-question-adversarial-20261102.md",lines.join("\n")+"\n");
