response.push("","## Item-by-item attack response","","Difficulty is predicted by this author, not measured from players. B10 is explicitly a foundational safety exception requiring manager/independent acceptance; no urgency sign is hidden. Context items remain linked/scaffolded and are not claimed to be independent syndrome questions.","","| ID | Original verdict | Author prediction | Cue / fairness / suggestion responses | Intended reasoning | Specific change | Residual lint |","|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|");
for(const i of packet){const n=i.reviewResponse.noteResponses;response.push("| "+[i.id,i.reviewResponse.originalVerdict,i.reviewResponse.selfCheck.difficulty,[n.cues.length,n.fairness.length,n.suggestions.length].join(" / "),i.inference,i.whatChanged,i.lint.after.map(f=>f.rule).join(", ")||"none"].map(cell).join(" | ")+" |");}
response.push("","## Construct boundaries for clinician review","","Stable IDs and all 370 concept definitions remain unchanged. B24 now applies the CD20/architecture limitation to obtaining adequate diagnostic material; B29 adds a related reversal/recovery issue to discharge/support planning; B28/B38 apply existing statistical distinctions to explicitly constructed calculations. B13-B16 use adverse malignant-polyp findings to test the same regional oncologic-resection objective. B36 selects adaptation of a mixed-outcome process test within its existing adopt/adapt/abandon objective. These application changes require Melissa's construct-equivalence review; if she considers an underlying learning meaning materially changed, create a new concept version before approval. No silent concept-version change or approval is claimed.","","Remaining warnings are retained with individual reasons in lintReview. They include conventional diagnosis-name length differences, real protocol abbreviations, coarse physiology-category mismatches, necessary raw observations and balanced plan/statistical combinations. Do not treat lower counts or a self-check as proof of difficulty or a valid key.");
